entity tree {
  name     = "tree"
  kind     = "block"
  summary  = "An indented file-tree diagram shape: one row per nested tree_node, with file-explorer connector guides."
  related  = [diagrams, icons]
  audience = :both
  body {
    p "`tree` renders an **indented file-tree**: one row per `tree_node`, indented by depth with the classic file-explorer connector guides drawn between a parent and its children. Each node carries a `title` (its positional label) plus an optional `icon` and `color`, and nodes nest arbitrarily, so it suits a directory layout, a config tree, or any hierarchy. A `tree` is a diagram shape, so it lives inside a `diagram` and is placed by `x` / `y` (or anchors)."
    code "wcl" { source = <<'SRC'
iconset lucide {}

diagram { width = 360  height = 220
  tree {
    tree_node "src/" {
      icon  = "folder"
      color = "#88c0d0"
      tree_node "render/" {
        icon = "folder"
        tree_node "svg.rs"  { icon = "file" }
        tree_node "html.rs" { icon = "file" }
      }
      tree_node "lib.rs"  { icon = "file" }
      tree_node "tree.rs" { icon = "file" }
    }
    tree_node "Cargo.toml" { icon = "file" }
  }
}
SRC
    }
    p "Icons resolve from any declared [iconset](entity_icons); a node's `color` is any CSS colour and themes its label and icon. Give a node an `id` to make it an edge target — an `edge` then attaches to that node's row (west / east), exactly like connecting any other shape."
  }
}
